        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Bangkok</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1400 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Founded</span><span class="info-stat-val">It is not known exactly when the area was first settled; a customs outpost under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> existed by the 15th century. The city dates its foundation as the capital to 21 April 1782, when King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama-i">Rama I</a> erected the city pillar on the east bank.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Where</span><span class="info-stat-val">In the delta of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chao-phraya-river">Chao Phraya River</a> in the central plain of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, about 25 km from the river's mouth on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-thailand">Gulf of Thailand</a>.</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Known for</span><span class="info-stat-val">A customs outpost of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a>; the siege of 1688 that expelled the French; Thonburi under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taksin">King Taksin</a>; the Rattanakosin capital of 1782; Siam's modernisation under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongkut">Mongkut</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chulalongkorn">Chulalongkorn</a>; its Chinese community; canals and floating houses; its place as the nation's political stage</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Today</span><span class="info-stat-val">Bangkok is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, governed as a special administrative area by the Bangkok Metropolitan Administration.</span></div>
